{"id":"n728b2a051a","headline":"US expands visa social media checks to three more categories from October 1","summary":"From October 1, the US will expand social media screening to I, TN and TD visa applicants, requiring profiles to be public or open. The regime already covers H-1B workers and students.","why":"Visa rules affect the movement of foreign journalists, professionals and students into the US, which matters for labour supply and business travel.","category":"geopolitics","event_type":"regulation","importance":1,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Washington, D.C.","country":"United States of America","lat":38.9,"lon":-77.0,"region":"na"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"The Economic Times","url":"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/nri/migrate/us-expands-visa-social-media-checks-to-three-more-categories-from-october-1/articleshow/134380530.cms"},"sources":[{"name":"The Economic Times","url":"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/nri/migrate/us-expands-visa-social-media-checks-to-three-more-categories-from-october-1/articleshow/134380530.cms"}],"published_at":"2026-09-21T05:22:50Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-12T06:29:12Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"6a9d4a0dd1a820fb","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-12T06:29:12Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-09-21T05:22:50Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-09-21T06:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"IN","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/parliament-government-building-4873983.jpg","alt":"parliament government building (illustration)","credit":"marcelkessler","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/federal-building-bern-federal-city-4873983/"}}